Date: Fri, 2 Jul 93 10:58:57 CDT
From: derek@cs.wisc.edu (Derek Zahn)
Subject: Logical Depth Machine Independence

Robin Hanson:

> This machine dependence issue has always been my main concern with the
> concept, and the rest of Tim's excerpt is silent on the subject.
> Anyone know how depth depends on the UTM, in general?

Bennett is dealing with "similar" UTMs.  In particular (I quote):

  The ability of universal turing machines to simulate one another
  efficiently implies a corresponding degree of machine-independence
  for depth:  for any two efficiently universal machines of the sort
  considered here, there exists a constant c and a linear polynomial
  L such that for any t, strings whose (s+c)-significant depth is at
  least L(t) on one machine will have s-significant depth at least t
  on the other.

Here 's-significant depth' refers to the logical depth given a
"compression factor" s.

derek


