They say that a black hole can be completely described by its mass,
angular momentum, and charge.  That's from the outside, of course, and
we are inside the universe (plus, the universe doesn't exactly seem like
a black hole), but it might be plausible to suppose that these parameters
suffice to describe the universe.  It might also be plausible to assume
that angular momentum and charge are both 0.

This would suggest that the log of the total mass of the universe in some
natural units (Planck masses?) might measure its information content.

