> * How few bits does it take to describe the state of the
> universe at time T?  In other words, what is the function
> "f" in states(T) = f (states(T0))?

In the Many-Worlds interpretation, which is deterministic, AIT would
suggest that the total information needed to describe the universe does
not change (although you might have to add bits to tell exactly what time
you were asking about).

In Copenhagen, each reduction of the wave function would add information
as you'd have to specify which way it went.  (This implies that the
information content of the universe is constantly increasing under the
conventional interpretation, in conflict with the general impression
that information disappears.)

