Now the bloodshed would be garish, for the thoughts that people cherish
Most and for which they would perish are their notions of what's real.
So as passions fan the flames, we all take sides and arms and aims
And cast aspersions, slurs and blames with wild enthusiastic zeal!

But the mailing list has rules for quenching those who lose their cools,
If they should show themselves such fools as not to let the battle be,
So faced with prospects sad and dismal of a self-destructive schism,
There's evolved a mechanism testing rationality:

>From a net concerned with law, in quest for facts and data raw,
>From which to tell of what he saw, there comes a sober-minded judge.
Although there's much research to do, and he has other interests, too,
Yet now his verdict's overdue -- and so perhaps he needs a nudge.

For masses eagerly await the resolution of debate
And plainly hope that he will state his findings soon, if not today.
While hapless pagans in the group must wonder if they're in the soup,
And 'neath a heavy burden stoop:

            They face the future -- come what May.


                                              -- Jay Freeman

